[0.188,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[48;5;237m                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m#21 Filter the reports by customer\u001b[39m                                                      \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mWhen I talk to one customer I only want their invoices. Add \u001b[38;5;153m--customer <id>\u001b[38;5;231m to \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;153msummary\u001b[38;5;231m and \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer aging\u001b[38;5;231m: with it, the report covers only that customer's invoices. \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mThe id is the customer's \u001b[38;5;153mid\u001b[38;5;231m in the file, such as \u001b[38;5;153macme\u001b[38;5;231m.\u001b[39m                                  \r\u001b[1B                              \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m- Without \u001b[38;5;153m--customer\u001b[38;5;231m, the reports print exactly what they print today.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- An \u001b[9Gd tha\u001b[15G no invoice has is an error that names the id.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;246mThought for \u001b[1m3s\u001b[22m, searched for \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m pattern, ran \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m●\u001b[39m Baseline noted: 1 pre-existing failure (\u001b[38;5;153mdiscounts.test.ts > takes WELCOME10 on an \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;153minvoice issued today\u001b[39m, date-related), 17 passing. Not mine to fix.\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m●\u001b[39m Reading tests and listing fixture files\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m  ⎿  \u001b[39m\u001b[2m\u001b[3mNow design the implementation. Requirements: - Add \u001b[38;5;153m--customer <id>\u001b[39m to \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3msummary\u001b[39m and \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer aging\u001b[39m. - With it, the report covers only that customer's \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Binvoices. - Without it, reports print exactly what they print today. - Unknown id is \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m\u001b[3man error naming the id. Where should filtering happen? Options: 1. In CLI: parse \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m   \u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3m--customer\u001b[39m, filter invoices, error if none match. 2. Add filtering to summarize/aging\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bfunctions. Cleanest: a small helper in cli.ts or a function in report? Filtering \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m\u001b[3minvoices by customer id is generic. I think a helper in cli.ts is fine, but \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m     \u001b[2m\u001b[3mtestability favors a function maybe. The tests currently only test summarize and \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Baging. We should add tests. How do tests invoke CLI? There's no CLI test currently. \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BWe can add unit tests for a filter function, but the requirement is…\r\u001b[2B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;174m✻\u001b[3GTwisting… \u001b[38;5;246m(33s · ↓\u001b[22G5.5k tokens · thought for 16s)\r\u001b[1B  ⎿  Tip: Use /btw\u001b[20Gto ask a quick\u001b[35Gside question without interrupting Claude's current work\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
